Yes, Mr. Governor.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:51.050
The Constitution of this state clearly says that all laws must be enacted by a majority of the representatives of the citizens of the state.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:56.200
Now, if Hooterville has had no representation in the State Assembly since 1922,

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:59.980
it seems to me that any laws passed since that time...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.770
are invalid. Well, if that's true, do you realize the chaos it would cause? Why, it would set the

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:10.740
state back for years, cost us millions. I'm not going to allow that. Well, now, Mr. Governor,

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:17.480
the people of Heaterville, the people of Hooterville have been deprived of their just rights. I agree.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:22.560
Now, the people have been deprived of representation all these years, and I do think that the state owes

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:27.390
them something. I feel that the people of Hooterville would be very well satisfied if you could arrange

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.830
a refund of all the taxes that they paid to the state.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:36.360
while they were without representation well i think that is a reasonable demand mr douglas

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:41.430
got yourself a deal well thank you sir thank you oh uh i have a little something here for you

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:44.740
it's a souvenir of your visit to the state capitol

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:49.340
put in your car you can use the pouch for a litter bag

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.280
Here you are, Jerry, Fred, Frank.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:05.550
Well, I'll be doggone.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:08.980
Look, Sam, I got back $400.22.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.560
I got $384.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:14.080
Oh, here's Mr. Douglas.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.700
Three cheers for Mr. Douglas.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.300
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:18.600
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:19.940
Hip, hip, hooray!

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:24.600
And when I walked up to that store, they cheered.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.370
Darling, I'm so proud of you.

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:28.790
Well, you deserve a lot of credit for what you did.

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:29.970
You mean for...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.520
I'm sleeping on the floor on that mattress.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.820
If it hadn't been for you, I wouldn't have had the appointment with the governor.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.110
Who was it you called?

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:41.140
The same lady who gave me the card for the discount house.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:43.350
He's, uh...

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:44.670
Mr. Douglas! Mr. Douglas!

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:44.970
What?

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:46.280
You'd better get out of town.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:46.600
Why?

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:49.240
They're gonna tar and feather you for getting that tax refund.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.300
Darling, I'm so proud of you.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:52.300
Proud?

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:56.400
Mr. Drucker's supplying the feathers, and they're getting up a collection for a barrel of tar.

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:57.630
I gave 50 cents.

00:19:58.410 --> 00:19:59.970
Do I have to give something to...

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.920
Would you mind telling me what you're talking about?

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.020
The tax refund.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.780
I thought they were happy about that.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:08.240
They were until they got the bill.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:09.090
Hot bell.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:10.530
The one the governor sent him.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:15.630
He said since the state's refunding the tax money, then we've got to pay for all the work they've done around here.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:17.810
$8,000 for road repair.

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:25.080
$9,000 for a bridge, $3,000 for a water tank, $222,000 for Hooderville High School.

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:29.910
Well, anyway, it comes to a grand total of $3,498,000.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.260
and 22 cents

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:32.540
what

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:36.850
Dividing that up between everybody in Hootaville, it comes to $600,000 apiece.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:38.670
That's ridiculous.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.180
They can't do this.

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:44.040
Long before this state was founded.

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:49.430
The American farmer laid down his rake and his hoe to take up the fight against tyranny and injustice.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.300
dumping tea into the Boston Harbor.

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:55.390
riding through every Middlesex village and farm.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.440
One is by land and two is by sea.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:02.800
And as the hoofbeats of Paul Revere's horse echoed through the streets,

00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:07.140
the American farmers came out of the houses, out of the farms, out of the...

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:07.580
Au revoir.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:08.260
What?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:09.830
Who is playing the five?

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:11.060
Thank you.
